t (Didgeridoo);28g 1s 7c;25g 8s 1c; A long, tubular wind instrument originating from Indigenous Australian cultures, played by blowing air through the mouthpiece while vibrating the lips.;Musical Instrument (Harp);53g 8s 4c;37g 5c; A large, stringed instrument with a triangular frame and multiple strings, played by plucking or strumming.;Musical Instrument (Sitar);96g 3c;71g 6c; A stringed instrument with a long neck and pear-shaped body, played by plucking or strumming.;Musical Instrument (Triangle);7s 6c;6s 5c; A small metal instrument shaped like a triangle, played by striking with a metal beater.;Musical Instrument (Tuba);115g 4s 8c;100g 6s 8c; A large brass instrument with a wide tube and flared bell, played by buzzing the lips into a mouthpiece.;Musical Instrument (Xylophone);9g 3s 3c;7g 8s 8c; A percussion instrument with wooden bars of different lengths, played by striking with mallets.;Onyx Goblet;26g 7s 9c;20g 7s 3c;--;Orb of Timekeeping;180g 3c;154g 4s; A crystal orb that accurately measures time, perfect for keeping track of hours and days.;Potion of Blur;252g 8c;237g 7s 9c;A clear ichor, contained in a faceted phial sealed with wax.;Potion of Cure Light Wounds;53g 4s 9c;40g 6s 1c;This smoky liquid smells like fresh bread.;Potion of Darkvision;236g 9s;185g 3s 6c;This glowing elixir causes shadows to appear darker when used.;Potion of Flying;736g 6c;601g 1s 4c;This potion grants the ability to fly for a limited duration when consumed.;Ring ofsell Turning;108215g 4c;69355g 2s 2c;(inscription provides clue to function) This polished ring also repels small insects when held.;Rod of Absorption;21596g 1s 1c;19078g 2s 5c;This rod can absorb and store magical energy, allowing its wielder to harness it later.;Rune-etched Gauntlets;185g 9s 2c;169g 1s 7c; Gauntlets inscribed with ancient runes that enhance the wearer's strength and combat prowess.;Sack of Apples;4g 2s 9c;3g 6s 9c;50 lb.Can be bought in fractions. 1g ;Staff of Abjuration (16 of 50 charges);16669g 6s;10440g 9s 3c;This masterwork staff is said to be imbued with thesirit of the renowned wizard Amrad, who slew the Leviathan of the Sea of Lauce. (design provides clue to function);Staff of Size Alteration;21926g 5s 5c;19058g 9s 1c;(27 of 50 charges) This elm staff once belonged to the legendary sorcerer Getema, who vanished in the Lair of the Wyrm Duke.;True Wand;27118g 9s 7c;20811g 4s 1c;This wand can be used as an arcane focus. If you can castsells with an arcane focus and use this wand for yoursells, yoursells require no material components that cost less than 1000g. Additionally, when you cast asell using this wand as your arcane focus, roll an ability check with yoursellcasting ability score. If you roll higher than 11 + thesell's level, you cast thesell without using asellslot. This fails if you have nosellslots remaining of thesell's level and therefore couldn't cast without succeeding.;Veil of Concealment;95g 1s 7c;71g 6c; A shimmering veil that obscures the wearer's features, granting them anonymity and protection.
